			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4479432">
									

<p>I'm not sure on the usage of Eire for Ireland. It's only been known by that name since 1937, and is officially known as Ireland in English, so that feels a little odd for a being born &quot;[s]ometime before 750 BC&quot;.</p>
<p>You might also want to consider Éire (instead of Eire), as eire (no accent) means a burden, and I've know a few Irish object to it on that basic (I've also known many who don't care, and it's sometimes omitted in Irish for uppercase anyway, such as on old stamps or ships).</p>

