														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4758621">
									

<p>I have to say, you had me at Cathbhadh and I wanted to give you all the doots by the end of his conversation with the new Administrator. I'm a major fan of a huge number of mythologies and loved watching this unfold.</p>
<p>Using the geode as an anchor was inspired and hints to me of the power of his bindings.</p>
<p>I was confused with how much destruction he was raining down but the conversation really tied it up well for me. He isn't a warmonger, but he will get the job done. He has had to watch too many of his people conquered or enslaved, to many of their civilizations destroyed.</p>
<p>I see his actions as being very controlled, it's more of a culling rather than wanton destruction. Pruning out the elements destined to cause the most impact, in a way guiding the remainder towards a less cohesive and effective organization, if not more moderate.</p>
<p>With his abilities I wouldn't be surprised if each of the deaths in those incidents were carefully selected.</p>
<p>Enthusiastic +1</p>

